## Item 4 — Checkout must REQUIRE account creation

Guest checkout is not allowed; an account must exist before an order
can be placed.

**Implementation:** enforced in code via `pre_option_*` filters in
`inc/woocommerce.php` (not wp-admin Accounts & Privacy settings, so a
settings edit on prod can never silently re-enable guest checkout):

- `woocommerce_enable_guest_checkout` → forced `no`
- `woocommerce_enable_signup_and_login_from_checkout` → forced `yes`
- `woocommerce_enable_checkout_login_reminder` → forced `yes`
- `woocommerce_registration_generate_username` → forced `yes`
  (username derived from billing email — "nothing too detailed")
- `woocommerce_registration_generate_password` → forced `no`
  (checkout always shows a visible required "Create account password"
  field; with both generation options on, WooCommerce hides the account
  section and creates accounts silently, which would not read as
  "account required" to a processor reviewer)

The RUO acknowledgment checkbox requirement is unchanged and was
verified to still render alongside the account fields.
